      "note": "Machine draft; semantic and native-speaker review pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "ingame.dlssnr-stagecontrols.but_it_can_only_change_what_the_game_and_this_st_eae8a17c",
      "surface": "in_game",
      "section": "dlssnr-stagecontrols",
      "control": "label",
      "english": "but it can only change what the game and this stage allow.",
      "context": "Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_StageControls.h",
      "placeholders": [],
      "preserve": [],
      "line_breaks": false,
      "revision": 1,
      "sources": [
        {
          "path": "OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_StageControls.h",
          "line": 130,
          "kind": "provider"
        }
      ],
      "translation": "mais elle ne peut modifier que ce que le jeu et cette étape autorisent.",
      "note": "Machine draft; semantic and native-speaker review pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "ingame.dlssnr-stagecontrols.native_temporal_works_within_the_game_s_upscaler_1e91b62c",
      "surface": "in_game",
      "section": "dlssnr-stagecontrols",
      "control": "paragraph",
      "english": "Native Temporal works within the game's upscaler, usually before super resolution. Some setups place it after reconstruction. It is usually more stable during motion, but it can only change what the game and this stage allow.\n\nPresent works on the final image after upscaling. It can add a stronger visual effect while remaining fast, but moving objects may flicker or ghost when the game does not provide usable motion information. It uses qualified depth and motion guides when available and image-only input otherwise.",
      "context": "Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_StageControls.h",
      "placeholders": [],
      "preserve": [],
      "line_breaks": true,
      "revision": 1,
      "sources": [
        {
          "path": "OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_StageControls.h",
          "line": 128,
          "kind": "presentation-binding"
        }
      ],
      "translation": "Native Temporal fonctionne dans l'upscaler du jeu, généralement avant la super résolution. Certaines configurations le placent après la reconstruction. Il est généralement plus stable en mouvement, mais il ne peut modifier que ce que le jeu et cette étape permettent.\n\nPresent fonctionne sur l'image finale après l'upscale. Il peut ajouter un effet visuel plus fort tout en restant rapide, mais les objets en mouvement peuvent scintiller ou créer des images fantômes lorsque le jeu ne fournit pas d'informations de mouvement utilisables. Il utilise des guides de profondeur et de mouvement qualifiés lorsqu'ils sont disponibles et une entrée basée uniquement sur l'image sinon.",
      "note": "Machine draft; semantic and native-speaker review pending."
    },
    {
      "id": "ingame.dlssnr-stagecontrols.native_temporal_works_within_the_game_s_upscaler_22fd3692",
